The Forecasting AlgorithmThe 
system calculates a Unified Success Score (USS) scaled from 0 to 100:
\(\text{USS}=(\text{Sentiment\ Score}\times 0.4)+ (\text{Historical\ Multiplier\ Score}\times 0.6)\)
Confidence Calculation:
Based on data density and source alignment. If sentiment and stats point to 
the same trajectory, confidence increases.
Risk Evaluation:
Calculated inversely to financial backing and market saturation flags.
Error Detection (Self-Correction):
The system logs an error_margin once actual box office data becomes available, 
adjusting its internal source weights if the margin exceeds 15%.
